  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The agreed compost routine permits several possible work periods, and a session needs two volunteers.\", \"decision\": \"How should compost-turning sessions be organized?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe coordinator posts paired compost work periods and invites volunteers to claim either place. An explicit two-person structure makes incomplete sessions visible.\nVolunteers form pairs first and then choose a compost work period together. The session time follows an already agreed partnership.\nVolunteers choose compost work periods individually, and the coordinator pairs overlapping choices. Pairs are assembled from existing availability."
    }
  ],
